          {
            "figure": "Figure 3",
            "page_1_based": 3,
            "caption": "Figure 3. Architecture illustrating the practical implementation of CIC . During a gradient update step, random τ = (s, s′) tuples are\nsampled from the replay buffer, then a particle estimator is used to compute the entropy and a noise contrastive loss to compute the\nconditional entropy. The contrastive loss is backpropagated through the entire architecture. The entropy and contrastive terms are then\nscaled and added to form the intrinsic reward. The RL agent is optimized with a DDPG (Lillicrap et al., 2016).",
